WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.723
Identify safe, lawful ways people can seek help when their rights are denied.

00:00:05.533 --> 00:00:10.370
Human rights protect dignity and fair treatment. The curriculum mentions speaking up,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.610
negotiation and asking institutions such as Social Welfare, CHRAJ, the police or law

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.819
courts for help.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.452
Children should first tell a trusted adult, teacher or appropriate child-protection

00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:27.636
service if they feel unsafe. Rights are exercised responsibly while respecting other

00:00:27.636 --> 00:00:28.068
people.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.494
Role-play telling a trusted teacher about unfair treatment and asking for help.
